WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.957
Entering a result from a paper report.

2
00:00:02.957 --> 00:00:07.851
Search for the person first, enter
a faxed lab result on their record,

3
00:00:07.851 --> 00:00:10.488
and read what MERIT did with it.

4
00:00:12.052 --> 00:00:16.428
A faxed lab report has arrived
for a child named Leo Rivera.

5
00:00:16.428 --> 00:00:22.809
Before entering anything, search for him,
so the result joins his existing record.

6
00:00:23.175 --> 00:00:25.848
Type the last name, then the first name.

7
00:00:25.848 --> 00:00:31.192
Adding the date of birth from the
report narrows the search to one person.

8
00:00:31.555 --> 00:00:35.317
One match, with the same
name and date of birth.

9
00:00:35.317 --> 00:00:36.971
Open his record.

10
00:00:37.332 --> 00:00:40.827
The person page shows who
he is and his history.

11
00:00:40.827 --> 00:00:42.830
Choose Enter a result.

12
00:00:43.195 --> 00:00:45.120
Choose the analyte first.

13
00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:48.600
The specimen and unit choices follow it.

14
00:00:48.956 --> 00:00:54.947
The report says the blood was drawn from
a vein, so set the sample type to venous.

15
00:00:55.302 --> 00:01:00.259
Type the value exactly
as reported: 4.2 µg/dL.

16
00:01:00.612 --> 00:01:04.545
Enter the date the blood was
collected, which is required,

17
00:01:04.545 --> 00:01:07.183
and the date the lab reported it.

18
00:01:07.550 --> 00:01:13.250
Add the test method, the lab's accession
number, and the reason for the test.

19
00:01:13.665 --> 00:01:19.481
For the laboratory, type part of its
name, then choose it from the list.

20
00:01:19.848 --> 00:01:24.875
Check the entries against the paper
report, then choose Save result.

21
00:01:25.232 --> 00:01:29.803
MERIT confirms the result, with the value
converted to its standard unit and the

22
00:01:29.803 --> 00:01:31.803
population it counts toward.

23
00:01:32.919 --> 00:01:37.416
Below it, MERIT lists each level
the result was compared with,

24
00:01:37.416 --> 00:01:40.790
and whether a case was opened or updated.

25
00:01:41.155 --> 00:01:47.413
From here, enter another result from the
same report, or go back to his record.

26
00:01:48.588 --> 00:01:53.603
In this video you searched by name and
date of birth before entering anything,

27
00:01:53.603 --> 00:01:58.875
entered the result on the existing person
record, and read the standardized value,

28
00:01:58.875 --> 00:02:02.682
the levels it was compared
with and the case outcome.
